@ atanh atanh/atanh.wc
# This file contains worst cases for atanh with at least 43 identical bits
# after the round bit (computed with BaCSeL with -m 44).
# Important notes:
# (1) since atanh(-x) = -atanh(x), if x is a worst case, then -x is too.
#     To save space, only positive numbers are included here.
# (2) for |x| < 0x1.d12ed0af1a27fp-27, atanh(x) rounds to x (to nearest)
#     thus only worst cases for x >= 0x1.d12ed0af1a27fp-27 are included
#     Proof: (a) for |x| < 2^-27, since the Taylor expansion of atanh(x) is
#     x + x^3/3 + O(x^5), the 2nd term satisfies (for x > 0):
#     x^3/3 < 2^-54 x/3 <= ulp(x)/6 since 2^-53 x < ulp(x).
