#
# the following was contributed by Bernt Gombala
# (file wc_targeted_search_result_cases.txt)
#
# Hard-to-round cases for binary64 pow(x,y) found by doing an
# optimized search that was done as follows:
#  * Pick a target value Z that is located exactly at a binary64 midpoint-value.
#  * Then, for each possible value of Y that can result in pow(x,y)=Z ending
#    up in the binary64 normal-number range, compute (or estimate by
#    interpolation) a value of X = pow(Z,1/Y), and check whether X is
#    very close to a representable binary64 number. If it is, round X to
#    binary64, then check how many identical bits after the round-bit the
#    resulting value of pow(x,y) has.
# The cases below were obtained by spending approx 1 CPU-year on a 3GHz
# intel core2 processor doing such a search for various values of Z
# close to 1. This identified 13317 near-midpoint cases where pow(x,y)
# has at least 100 identical bits after the round-bit - the worst such
# cases found have 117 identical bits.
#
